{
  "_comment_1": "APPLIES WHEN THIS ROOT IS WATCHED. watchman reads .watchmanconfig at watch time. The dev-hermit root watch was removed during the 2026-09-21 recovery and should remain absent unless a consumer genuinely needs it; a later watch will load these exclusions.",
  "_comment_2": "WHY: worktrees/ and ignored/ contain machine-local worktrees, validation checkouts, logs, and build outputs. On 2026-09-21, crawling ignored/validate left watchman unfinished after 16 million entries, pinned its 15 GiB cgroup, consumed more than 30 GiB of swap, exhausted inotify, and contributed to 457 service restarts.",
  "_comment_3": "This fixes the CAUSE, not the detector. release-worktree.rs is deliberately unchanged (zero-line diff) so its sensitivity to a genuine occupant is unaltered by construction rather than by careful edit. Do NOT 'fix' that check by excluding the release's own paths: the offending fd was inside the tree being released, so excluding the proof paths makes the predicate vacuous. Verified on a disposable root that this config parses (unknown _comment keys are accepted) and that ignore_dirs really excludes worktrees/ from query results.",
  "ignore_dirs": ["worktrees", "ignored"]
}
